<title>USA: High Plains Wheat - Basis bids mostly unchanged.</title>
<headline>High Plains Wheat - Basis bids mostly unchanged.</headline>
<dateline>KANSAS CITY, Mo. 1996-12-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Basis bids for hard red winter wheat were mostly unchanged as movement stayed slack, grain merchandisers in the U.S. High Plains said Wednesday.</p>
<p>&quot;I think marketing of grain is going to be real slow until the first of the year,&quot; a dealer in southern Kansas said. &quot;For tax purposes, farmers don't want the income until then.&quot;</p>
<p>Basis bids were unchanged at most locations in the country, although in Houston, one export firm had lowered its bid by two cents per bushel.  </p>
